            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0807" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">846G.79693/4–1548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-04-15T17:00:00+08:00">April 15, 1948—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 17—4:24 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>678. Embassy learns Minister Commerce [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Communications</hi>] expecting reply to his plea regarding Hong
                    Kong–Shanghai air traffic reported Embtel 608 of April 5. Please confirm
                    Embassy’s assumption Department instruction contained Deptel 439 of March 24
                    remains in force.</p>
                <p>Repeated Shanghai 278.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
